{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Backing Out", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Need + Passive Infinitive and Need +Verb+ing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">need + passive infinitive</span> and <span class=\"italic\">need +verb+ing</span> to talk about things that need to be done. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use these structures to focus on the <span class=\"strong\">thing</span> that needs doing, not the person who is doing it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + Need + Passive Infinitive", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">My blog article <span class=\"strong\">needs to be wrapped up</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The subject of the sentence is the thing that needs doing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + Need + Verb + ing", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The floor <span class=\"strong\">needs washing</span></span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use <span class=\"italic\">need</span> with a gerund (v-ing), it has a passive meaning. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My blog article needs to be wrapped up. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My Visa card needs to be paid off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The floors need washing, and the carpet needs vacuuming. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My clothes need to be washed.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Causative - Get/Have - Solving Problems", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use a <span class=\"italic\">causative</span> verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the causative verbs get/have when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">My boss <span class=\"strong\">had me do</span> an emergency project.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this sentence the boss asks or persuades you to do an emergency project.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the causative is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "have + object + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had the axe-throwing club sign us up</span> yesterday.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "or ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + get + object + Infinitive ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Maybe you can <span class=\"strong\">get him to change</span> his mind.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">get</span> to convey the idea that you need to <span class=\"underline\">persuade someone to do something</span>.<br> <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral and implies that you give someone the responsibility to do something.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "He said that his boss had him doing some emergency project where he had to write a press release.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am having trouble getting other people to attend. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had the axe-throwing club sign us up yesterday, so I can't back out now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I can get him to come out. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think I can also get some people I know to take part as well.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tied up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "occupied or engaged", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Maybe he is tied up at his new job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about negative feelings towards a friend.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "press release", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a statement or announcement about something newsworthy that is released to the press or media", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He had to write a press release.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to avoid doing something that you do not want to do, or to escape responsibility", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is just trying to get out of it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to back out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decide not to do something that you had said you would do", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't back out now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "intrigued", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something or someone that captures your attention and inspires curiosity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was intrigued by their story.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "at the end of my rope", "type": "name"}, {"content": "out of energy or patience", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm at the end of my rope with Peter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm different kinds of parties and party activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, choose a party or an activity and make a plan and a schedule.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the things do you need to do beforehand. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use need + passive ing, and need + passive to describe all the things that need to be done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use expressions with have/get to say how to do things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Plan your guest list of friends to invite. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Pick five friends and explain to your partner why they are fun to have at a party.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm about different parties and party activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use \u2018need + passive ing' and \u2018need + passive to' to discuss things that need to be done before the party.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express activities other people have to get or have. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss friends and explain why they would be good guests.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le18ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le18ob05re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le18ob05re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob05re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Let's see. What do I need to do for this weekend? My blog article needs to be wrapped up. My Visa card needs to be paid off. The floors need washing. The carpet needs vacuuming. Hmm. What else? My clothes need to be washed and then \u2026 <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Hello?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: Hi, Sally. It's Vanessa. I'm furious right now. I want to kill Peter!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Why? What happened?<br />", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob05re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: He canceled on the axe throwing. I'm so mad!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: No! What did he say?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: Nothing. He texted me. He came up with some lame excuse.  He said that his boss had him doing some emergency project where he had to write a press release. I phoned him back, but he didn't answer, so I left a message.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Well, maybe that's true. Maybe he is tied up at his new job.<br />", "id": 2, "time": "30900"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob05re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: How long does that take to write a stupid press release? He is just trying to get out of it.  Also, I am having trouble getting other people to attend. I had the axe-throwing club sign us up yesterday, so I can't back out. Sally, I'm at the end of my rope with Peter. Can I get you to call him? Maybe you can get him to change his mind.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Sure. I'll talk to him. I can get him to come out. I think I can also get some people I know to take part as well. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: Really? Oh. That's good news.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Yeah, I talked to them today and they sounded intrigued.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: This is really starting to stress me out.<br />", "id": 3, "time": "56500"}]}}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, personal qualities and behavior.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that need to be done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about solving problems. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What kind of events do you enjoy attending?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Have you ever organized an event? What kind?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Have you ever backed out of going to an event? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Why did you cancel?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Peter <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">backed out</span> on plans. Can you believe he canceled?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "To <span class=\"italic\">\u201cback out\u201d</span> means to withdraw from a previous commitment. ", "tip_id": 0, "type": "text"}], "type": "tips"}], "id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [2]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DMC", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "to attend a press event.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "to write a press release.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}, {"text": "", "id": 2, "_data": [{"content": "to write a press excuse.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"text": "", "id": 3, "_data": [{"content": "other plans.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"text": "", "id": 4, "_data": [{"content": "no excuse.", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "Peter came up with a lame excuse. He has ...", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "objective"}], "id": 0}, {"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "Sally", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "Peter", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"text": "", "id": 2, "_data": [{"content": "Vanessa", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}, {"text": "", "id": 3, "_data": [{"content": "David", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"text": "", "id": 4, "_data": [{"content": "John", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "Who's angry?", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "objective"}], "id": 1}, {"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "Because she is sad", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_d